# ::tok The Prime Minister and the Ministers of Foreign Affairs, Health, Internal affairs, Tourism and Transportation agreed that starting Sunday, January 9, 2022, the entry of vaccinated/recovered foreigners (as defined by the Ministry of Health) from orange countries will be allowed—subject to filling out an online form ahead of time, performing a PCR or antigen test before boarding the plane, performing a PCR test upon entering Israel followed by entering isolation for 24 hours or receiving a negative test result (whichever comes first).
